{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1673811293"}, "name":{"label":"Its_theoo"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-08-14T10:38:11-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"9.1.72"}, "id":{"label":"14427618184"}, "title":{"label":"Favorite music and podcast app"}, "content":{"label":"I much prefer Spotify over other streaming apps like iTunes or Pandora. The only thing I that could improve is being able to remove ads from podcasts with premium.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=324684580&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id191410013"}, "name":{"label":"elad.ams"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-08-14T10:36:14-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"2"}, "im:version":{"label":"9.1.72"}, "id":{"label":"14427612159"}, "title":{"label":"DJ features is not a fit for 2026"}, "content":{"label":"Spotify DJ currently feels repetitive, predictable, and not particularly intelligent. It often cycles through similar artists, songs, and listening patterns instead of behaving like a DJ that genuinely understands context, mood, discovery, or how my taste evolves.\n\nI think the feature needs a fundamental rethink rather than incremental improvements. A great AI DJ should surprise me intelligently: understand what I’ve been listening to too much, recognize when I’m probably ready for something different, connect genres and artists in interesting ways, rediscover music I’ve forgotten, and introduce new tracks with a clear reason for why they fit.\n\nRight now, it feels much closer to a playlist with occasional commentary than an intelligent DJ. The potential is huge, but the experience needs substantially more variety, memory, contextual awareness, and willingness to explore beyond obvious recommendations.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=324684580&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1607138373"}, "name":{"label":"EvanHz"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-08-14T10:32:31-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"9.1.72"}, "id":{"label":"14427600683"}, "title":{"label":"Worst music streaming app oat"}, "content":{"label":"Spotify used to play 1-3 songs before interrupting with a short ad break (about 3 ads) , but recently its become 1 song and 5 ads following. It’s absolutely ridiculous that the free version of the app is this horrible of a user experience. \nAdding onto this, user safety is hardly a concern as the blocking feature does little to nothing and theres no way to personalize your ads, while at work you could receive an ad at any moment discussing completely inappropriate topics and theres no way to change that as pressing “not interested” also does nothing for you. Not to mention the fact that deranged people like D4vd are able to have a platform on the app, and spotify has done nothing to demonetize him.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=324684580&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
